            <ArticleTitle>Successful use of the right brachial approach to perform directional atherectomy of the left coronary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>45-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Although directional coronary atherectomy permits the treatment of complex coronary lesions, its use is limited in patients with peripheral vascular disease by the need to use a large guiding catheter. We describe a patient in whom the right brachial approach was successfully used to perform atherectomy of a semi-protected left main coronary stenosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
